<title>BELGIUM: German official confirms doubts over EMU pact.</title>
<headline>German official confirms doubts over EMU pact.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German economic state secretary Johannes Ludewig said on Monday it was unclear whether the European Union will reach agreement soon on a budget stability pact for countries inside monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;We will see whether it will happen this year,&quot; Ludewig, a close aide of Chancellor Helmut Kohl, told journalists ahead of a meeting of EU finance ministers.</p>
<p>Agreement on an accord enforcing budgetary rigour among governments joining a single currency has remained elusive due in part to renewed German demands for stricter rules.</p>
<p>- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
